Builds and reproduces backends from public commits and checks signed deployment policies; does not show what a live server runs

Usage: leptoskit verify <COMMAND>

Commands:
  approve-backend  Independently approve the exact bytes of a backend image descriptor
  build            Builds a backend bundle from a Git commit in a container without network access, twice, and requires identical executables
  reproduce        Rebuilds a pinned bundle from its own source and dependencies and compares the executable; also compares the source with its Git commit
  keygen           Writes a new deployment signing key and prints its public key
  sign             Signs a deployment policy naming the origins and releases a deployment serves
  deployment       Checks an origin's signed deployment policy against a key you trust. Does not show what its server runs
  record           Records the files in a prepared backend bundle. This does not build, sign, or attest the bundle
  check            Checks every bundle entry against an inventory with a separately trusted SHA-256. Does not contact or verify a running server
  help             Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version
